        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481421436",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": false,
        "description": "**Company Description** \n Altizam, derived from an Arabic word meaning “commitment,” is dedicated to innovation, development, and services in engineering, networking, and safety. Established in 2012 with a focus on networking and hardware solutions, the company expanded in 2018 to include safety, security systems, and industrial instrumentation. The organization emphasizes high\\-quality, reliable solutions and long\\-term partnerships with clients across diverse industries.\n \n\n\n\n**Role Description** \n This is a fulltime Frontend Developer role based in Karachi. The Frontend Developer will implement user\\-facing features, translate UI/UX designs into responsive web interfaces, and ensure cross\\-browser and cross\\-device compatibility. Day\\-to\\-day tasks include collaborating with designers and backend developers, maintaining and optimizing existing front\\-end codebases, and participating in code reviews and testing to ensure performance and accessibility. The role also involves troubleshooting UI issues, contributing to documentation, and supporting continuous improvement of web applications and internal tools.\n \n\n\n\n**Qualifications** \n\n\n\n* Strong Front\\-End Development skills, including modern HTML, CSS, and JavaScript frameworks or libraries (e.g., React, Next, etc.).\n* Experience with Responsive Web Design and cross\\-browser compatibility, ensuring consistent user experiences across devices.\n* Strong capabilities in Claude.ai, Codex with proven track record.\n* Must have experience in Agile development and Stand\\-ups / reporting. (Jira, ClickUp, Notion)\n* Must have experienced in SaaS product development\n* Solid understanding of Web Development principles and best practices, including performance optimization and accessibility.\n* Familiarity with Back\\-End Web Development or APIs to effectively integrate front\\-end components with server\\-side logic.\n* Background in Software Development, including version control (e.g., Git), debugging, and writing clean, maintainable code.\n* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related field, or equivalent practical experience.",
